Below is a focused C# example that uses Autodesk Advance Steel’s .NET API to add Cartesian (ordinate) dimensions for all round holes of a plate in a single-part drawing view, with the dimension origins set relative to the plate’s bottom-left corner (0,0). The sample shows how to locate the plate and its holes from the model, create a single-part drawing (if needed), open the detail view, and place Advance Steel Drawing dimension objects as Cartesian. Inline comments reference relevant API classes/methods.

Notes
- This example uses Advance Steel Drawing API objects (not plain AutoCAD ordinate dimensions) so they remain native to Advance Steel detailing. Key namespaces include Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Modeler, Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.DocumentManagement, Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Drawing, Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Modelling, Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.DotNetRoots, and Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.CADAccess.
- You can adapt the selection and filtering logic to your environment. The sample assumes a single plate with round holes (round contours) and demonstrates iterating holes and generating Cartesian dimensions from the plate’s bottom-left corner.
- Run the command after the model is open in Advance Steel. If a drawing isn’t created yet, the sample shows how to create a single-part drawing; otherwise it attaches to an existing one.

C# code (place in an Advance Steel plugin project; add references to the Advance Steel .NET assemblies)

using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Autodesk.AutoCAD.Runtime;               // CommandMethod
using Autodesk.AutoCAD.ApplicationServices;   // Application
using Autodesk.AutoCAD.DatabaseServices;      // ObjectId
using Autodesk.AutoCAD.EditorInput;           // Editor
using Autodesk.AutoCAD.Geometry;              // Point3d, Vector3d
// Advance Steel namespaces
using Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.CADAccess;        // AsDmDatabase, AstUIEnvironment
using Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.DocumentManagement; // DrawingProcess, DocumentManager
using Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.DotNetRoots;      // Transaction, DatabaseManager
using Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Modelling;        // Plate, Beam, Hole features
using Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Modeler;          // Model objects, Utilities
using Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Drawing;          // Drawing, View, Dimension classes

public class PlateHoleCartesianDims
{
  // Entry point command registered in Advance Steel
  [CommandMethod("AS_CARTESIAN_HOLE_DIMS")] 
  public void CreateHoleCartesianDimensions()
  {
    var acadDoc = Application.DocumentManager.MdiActiveDocument;
    var ed = acadDoc?.Editor;

    // Ensure Advance Steel database context
    using (var db = DatabaseManager.OpenCurrentDatabase())
    using (var tr = db.StartTransaction())
    {
      try
      {
        // 1) Find a target plate in the model (you can replace with object selection)
        //    API: DatabaseManager.GetAllObjects / filter by type Plate
        var allObjs = db.GetAllObjects();
        var plate = allObjs.OfType<Plate>().FirstOrDefault();
        if (plate == null)
        {
          ed?.WriteMessage("\nNo Plate found in model. Select a plate first or create one.");
          tr.Commit();
          return;
        }

        // 2) Get round hole features of the plate
        //    API: Plate.GetFeatures(), FeatureHole, FeatureRoundHole
        var features = plate.GetFeatures();
        var roundHoles = new List<FeatureRoundHole>();
        foreach (var feat in features)
        {
          if (feat is FeatureRoundHole rh)
            roundHoles.Add(rh);
        }
        if (roundHoles.Count == 0)
        {
          ed?.WriteMessage("\nSelected plate has no round holes.");
          tr.Commit();
          return;
        }

        // 3) Ensure a single-part drawing exists for the plate (or create one)
        //    API: DrawingProcess.CreateSinglePartDrawing(Plate)
        Drawing spDrawing = FindExistingSinglePartDrawing(plate) ??
                            DrawingProcess.CreateSinglePartDrawing(plate);
        if (spDrawing == null)
        {
          ed?.WriteMessage("\nFailed to create or find a single-part drawing for the plate.");
          tr.Commit();
          return;
        }

        // 4) Get the main view of the single-part drawing for the plate
        //    API: Drawing.GetViews(), View properties
        var view = spDrawing.GetViews().FirstOrDefault();
        if (view == null)
        {
          ed?.WriteMessage("\nNo view found in the single-part drawing.");
          tr.Commit();
          return;
        }

        // 5) Compute the bottom-left origin (0,0) on the plate in the view’s 2D coordinate system
        //    API: Plate.GetExtentsOnView(View), return min/max and transform helpers
        //    We convert model points to view 2D using View.WorldToView()
        var outline2d = GetPlateOutline2dOnView(plate, view, out var viewPlane);
        if (outline2d == null || outline2d.Count == 0)
        {
          ed?.WriteMessage("\nCould not compute plate outline on the view.");
          tr.Commit();
          return;
        }
        var minX = outline2d.Min(p => p.X);
        var minY = outline2d.Min(p => p.Y);
        var origin2d = new Point2d(minX, minY); // bottom-left corner in view coordinates

        // 6) For each round hole, get its center in model, convert to view 2D, then place Cartesian dimensions
        //    API: FeatureRoundHole.Center (model 3D), View.WorldToView(Point3d)
        //         DimensionCartesian (Advance Steel drawing dimension), with X/Y baseline from origin2d
        foreach (var hole in roundHoles)
        {
          Point3d centerModel = hole.Center; // 3D center in model coordinates
          Point2d center2d = ToView2d(view, centerModel);

          // Create a Cartesian dimension for X (horizontal) from origin (0,0) to hole center
          // API: DimensionCartesian constructor and properties
          var dimX = new DimensionCartesian(view)
          {
            Mode = DimensionCartesian.CartesianMode.X, // X ordinate
            Origin = origin2d,
            Target = center2d,
            TextPrefix = "X=",
            StyleName = "Standard" // adjust to your AS dim style
          };
          dimX.Create();

          // Create a Cartesian dimension for Y (vertical) from origin to hole center
          var dimY = new DimensionCartesian(view)
          {
            Mode = DimensionCartesian.CartesianMode.Y, // Y ordinate
            Origin = origin2d,
            Target = center2d,
            TextPrefix = "Y=",
            StyleName = "Standard"
          };
          dimY.Create();
        }

        ed?.WriteMessage($"\nCreated Cartesian dimensions for {roundHoles.Count} hole(s) relative to bottom-left (0,0).\n");
        tr.Commit();
      }
      catch (System.Exception ex)
      {
        ed?.WriteMessage("\nError: " + ex.Message);
        tr.Abort();
      }
    }
  }

  // Helper: Try to find an existing single-part drawing for a plate
  // API: DocumentManager, Drawing, Drawing.GetModelObjects()
  private Drawing FindExistingSinglePartDrawing(Plate plate)
  {
    foreach (var drw in DocumentManager.GetDrawings())
    {
      var objs = drw.GetModelObjects();
      if (objs != null && objs.Any(o => o.Equals(plate)))
        return drw;
    }
    return null;
  }

  // Helper: Convert a 3D model point to 2D view point
  // API: View.WorldToView(Point3d)
  private Point2d ToView2d(View view, Point3d modelPt)
  {
    var v2d = view.WorldToView(modelPt); // returns Point2d in the view’s plane
    return new Point2d(v2d.X, v2d.Y);
  }

  // Helper: Get the plate outer contour projected to the view as 2D points
  // API: Plate.GetOuterContour(), View.WorldToView(Point3d)
  private List<Point2d> GetPlateOutline2dOnView(Plate plate, View view, out Plane viewPlane)
  {
    viewPlane = view.GetViewPlane();
    var outline = new List<Point2d>();

    // Get outer contour vertices in model coordinates (assuming ordered loop)
    var outer = plate.GetOuterContour(); // returns a contour/loop; iterate vertices
    foreach (var v in outer.GetVertices())
    {
      var p3 = new Point3d(v.X, v.Y, v.Z);
      var p2 = view.WorldToView(p3);
      outline.Add(new Point2d(p2.X, p2.Y));
    }
    return outline;
  }
}

Usage steps
1) Build and load the plugin in Advance Steel (add references to the Advance Steel .NET assemblies from the SDK/installation).
2) Open a model with a plate containing round holes.
3) Run AS_CARTESIAN_HOLE_DIMS from the command line in Advance Steel.
4) If a single-part drawing for the plate does not exist, the command will create one; otherwise it uses the first available view.
5) The command places two Cartesian dimensions (X and Y) from the plate’s bottom-left corner (0,0) to each hole center.

Key Advance Steel API classes/methods referenced
- Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Modelling.Plate: GetFeatures(), GetOuterContour()
- Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Modelling.FeatureRoundHole: Center
- Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Drawing.DrawingProcess: CreateSinglePartDrawing(Plate)
- Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Drawing.Drawing: GetViews(), GetModelObjects()
- Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Drawing.View: WorldToView(Point3d), GetViewPlane()
- Autodesk.AdvanceSteel.Drawing.DimensionCartesian: Mode, Origin, Target, Create()

Additional resources
- Autodesk Advance Steel .NET API documentation (installed with SDK)
- ADN (Autodesk Developer Network) articles on Advance Steel Drawing and Modelling APIs
