SOLAR SYSTEM SIMULATION: STEP‑BY‑STEP GUIDE (HTML/CSS/JavaScript)

This guide builds a simple, performant 2D solar system visualization in the browser using Canvas. It includes:
- Clear steps with concrete code snippets (HTML, CSS, JS)
- Exactly how to fetch and parse astrophysical data (semimajor axes, orbital periods, radii) from NASA/JPL sources
- How those data map to simulation parameters (distance scaling, animation speeds)

Credible astrophysical data sources (NASA/JPL)
- NASA Planetary Fact Sheet (Metric) – semimajor axes (a), orbital periods (P), radii (R):
  https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/planetfact_table_m.html
- JPL SSD HORIZONS API (optional high‑fidelity ephemerides):
  https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/api/horizons.api
- JPL SSD Planetary Physical Parameters (reference):
  https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/phys_par.html

